-- A refusal is a determinate answer, so `l4 run` on this file exits 0 — unlike
-- a raising #ASSERT, which exits 1. The two must not be conflated.

GIVETH A NUMBER
`this case is not modelled` MEANS REFUSE "this case is not modelled"

#EVAL `this case is not modelled`
#ASSERT REFUSED `this case is not modelled`
#ASSERT `this case is not modelled` EQUALS 1
